          <xs:documentation>Direct Support. Furnish close and continuous fire support to a single maneuver element.</xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
      </xs:enumeration>
      <xs:enumeration value="GS">
        <xs:annotation>
          <xs:documentation>General Support. General Support (GS) units support the entire force. (They remain under the control of the force Field Artillery (FA) headquarters and are not committed to any subordinate element of the force.)</xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
      </xs:enumeration>
      <xs:enumeration value="GSR">
        <xs:annotation>
          <xs:documentation>General Support Reinforcing. General Support-Reinforcing (GSR) units support the entire force and augment the fires of designated force FA units when not providing gs fires. (GSR units are controlled by the force FA headquarters and are not committed to subordinate elements of the force.)</xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
      </xs:enumeration>
      <xs:enumeration value="R">
        <xs:annotation>
          <xs:documentation>Reinforcing. Reinforcing is a tactical mission that causes one FA unit to augment the fires of another FA unit that cannot provide sufficient fires for the supported force.</xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
      </xs:enumeration>
    </xs:restriction>
