      </xs:extension>
    </xs:simpleContent>
  </xs:complexType>
  <xs:simpleType name="GEOREFCentiminuteSimpleType">
    <xs:annotation>
      <xs:documentation>A data type for a location based on the world Geographic Reference System (GEOREF).</xs:documentation>
    </xs:annotation>
    <xs:restriction base="xs:string">
      <xs:pattern value="([A-HJ-NP-Z][A-HJ-M])([A-HJ-NPQ]{2})([0-5][0-9])([0-9]{2})([0-5][0-9])([0-9]{2})">
        <xs:annotation>
          <xs:documentation>The first element is a pair of letters representing the 15-degree quadrilateral; the first letter of the pair allows the letters A to Z, omitting I and O; the second letter of the pair allows the letters A to M, omitting I and O. The second element is a pair of letters representing a 1-degree quadrilateral within the 15-degree quadrilateral and allows the letter values A to H, J to N, P or Q. The third element is a 2-digit number representing the easting coordinate to the closest one minute, in values from 00 to 59. The fourth element is a 2-digit number representing one of the 100 equal parts of a minute of angle, in values from 00 to 99. The fifth element is a 2-digit number representing the northing coordinate to the closet one minute, in values from 00 to 59. The sixth element is a 2-digit number representing one of the 100 equal parts of a minute of angle, in values from 00 to 99.</xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
      </xs:pattern>
    </xs:restriction>
  </xs:simpleType>
  <xs:complexType name="GEOREFCentiminuteType">
    <xs:annotation>
      <xs:documentation>A data type for a location based on the world Geographic Reference System (GEOREF).</xs:documentation>
    </xs:annotation>
    <xs:simpleContent>
      <xs:extension base="usmtf:GEOREFCentiminuteSimpleType">
        <xs:attributeGroup ref="structures:SimpleObjectAttributeGroup"/>
      </xs:extension>
    </xs:simpleContent>
  </xs:complexType>
  <xs:simpleType name="GlobalAreaReferenceSystemSimpleType">
    <xs:annotation>
      <xs:documentation>A data type for a standard reference system authorized for reporting and referencing 30x30, 15x15, and 5x5 minute areas.</xs:documentation>
    </xs:annotation>
    <xs:restriction base="xs:string">
      <xs:pattern value="(00[1-9]|0[1-9][0-9]|[1-6][0-9][0-9]|7[0-1][0-9]|720)([A-H]|[J-N]|[P-Q])([A-H]|[J-N]|[P-Z])([1-4]|[1-4][1-9]){0,1}">
        <xs:annotation>
          <xs:documentation>The areas described by GARS are coincident with even WGS-84 degree and minute lines. The areas are read right (west to east, 001-720) then up (south to north, AA-QZ). The 30 minute by 30 minute areas are subdivided by quadrant into 15 minute by 15 minute areas (1-4), then further subdivided by a keypad division into 5 minute by 5 minute areas (1-9).</xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
      </xs:pattern>
    </xs:restriction>
  </xs:simpleType>
