    <xs:restriction base="xs:string">
      <xs:pattern value="[\-,A-Z0-9]{1,14}">
        <xs:annotation>
          <xs:documentation>One to six numerics denote one image number. Multiple image numbers are indicated by separating the image numbers by a comma. A sequence of images may be indicated by separating the first and last image numbers by a hyphen. One or more individual image numbers and a range of image numbers together may be indicated. If multiple frame numbers are referenced, enter best frame first. Leading zeros are permitted but not required for image numbers. Example: 500,490-510. No individual image number will exceed six characters. For further U.S. implementation guidance, see Repository of USMTF Program Items Document, item 77.</xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
      </xs:pattern>
    </xs:restriction>
  </xs:simpleType>
