    <xs:restriction base="xs:string">
      <xs:pattern value="[\.0-9]{1,12}">
        <xs:annotation>
          <xs:documentation>Each naval task echelon is identified by a one (seldom) or two (usually) digit number. Each naval task echelon number is separated by a decimal indicator. The first two digits represent the Numbered Fleet (1st digit) and Task Force (2nd digit). The next two digits represent the Task Group. The next two digits represent the Task Unit, and the last two digits represent the Task Element. When only one digit is assigned to a Task Echelon, the zero may be dropped and blank spaces are never permitted. An example of the task organization echelon number for the 2nd TASK ELEMENT of the 11th TASK UNIT of the 3rd TASK GROUP in the 6th TASK FORCE of the 7th FLEET would be written: "76.3.11.2" or "76.03.11.02".</xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
      </xs:pattern>
    </xs:restriction>
