      <xs:pattern value="[0-9]{2,2}(C|L|R){0,1}">
        <xs:annotation>
          <xs:documentation>The first two characters (digits) identify the magnetic heading required to land on the runway, rounded to the nearest 10 degrees. The third character (alphabetic) is used if there are parallel runways to indicate "R" for right, "L" for left or "C" for center runway, otherwise this character position is not used.</xs:documentation>
