        <xs:annotation>
          <xs:documentation>Data Link Coordination Net. A net used by the Interface Control Officer (ICO) to manage and coordinate the entire multi-TDL interface. The ICO uses this net to direct all changes to the OPTASK LINK, to include entry and exit of units, approving filter used, reconfiguration of the interface, changes to the DLRP, frequencies, or link duties, etc. The ICO is net control station for this net.</xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
      </xs:enumeration>
      <xs:enumeration value="TSN">
        <xs:annotation>
          <xs:documentation>Track Supervision Net. A net used by track surveillance personnel for the control and coordination of procedures used to maintain a clear tactical picture and to assist units entering or exiting the interface. The track data controller is net control station for this net.</xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
      </xs:enumeration>
      <xs:enumeration value="VPN">
        <xs:annotation>
          <xs:documentation>Voice Product Net. A net used to provide amplifying Signals Intelligence (SIGINT) information to interface units on a timely basis, and is used to coordinate sigint information reported on the interface. The Special Information Systems (SIS) manager is the net control station of this net.</xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
      </xs:enumeration>
    </xs:restriction>
  </xs:simpleType>
